4.5 The Contractor shall invoice the Client for Additional Services upon completion of the relevant work, and such invoices shall be payable within thirty (30) days of the date of invoice. Where Additional Services are anticipated to exceed INR 2,00,000 in aggregate in any Contract Year, the Contractor shall obtain the Client's prior written approval before commencing such work.

4.6 All amounts payable under this Agreement are exclusive of Goods and Services Tax (GST) and any other applicable taxes, levies, or duties. The Contractor shall raise invoices showing GST separately, and the Client shall be entitled to avail input tax credit in accordance with applicable law.

4.7 The Client shall have the right to withhold payment of any amount disputed in good faith, provided that the Client notifies the Contractor in writing of the dispute within fifteen (15) days of receipt of the relevant invoice and the parties use reasonable endeavours to resolve the dispute within thirty (30) days. Any undisputed portion of the invoice shall be paid in accordance with Clause 4.3.

4.8 The Annual Fee shall be reviewed at the commencement of each Contract Year. Any adjustment shall be based on the Wholesale Price Index (WPI) published by the Office of the Economic Adviser, Government of India, and shall not exceed ten percent (10%) of the Annual Fee for the preceding Contract Year, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the parties.

5. SCOPE OF SERVICES

5.1 The Contractor shall provide the Services at the Sites listed in Annexure A, which include the following categories:

(a) Energy monitoring and reporting, including installation, commissioning, and maintenance of energy meters and data loggers;

(b) Analysis of energy consumption data and identification of efficiency improvement opportunities;

(c) Preparation and submission of monthly energy consumption reports, and quarterly energy performance reviews;

(d) Recommending and, where agreed, implementing energy conservation measures;

(e) Conducting periodic energy audits, at least once per Contract Year, at each Site;

(f) Providing training to the Client's facility staff on energy management best practices; and

(g) Such other services as may be agreed between the parties in writing from time to time.

5.2 The detailed scope of work, including deliverable formats and reporting timelines, is set out in the Statement of Work attached as Annexure B. In the event of any inconsistency between this Agreement and the Statement of Work, the terms of this Agreement shall prevail.

5.3 The Contractor shall assign a dedicated Account Manager who shall be the single point of contact for the Client. The Account Manager shall be available during business hours on all working days and shall respond to the Client's queries within two (2) business days.

5.4 The Contractor shall maintain all equipment installed at the Sites in good working order. Any equipment failure shall be attended to within forty-eight (48) hours of notification by the Client, and the Contractor shall provide a temporary replacement or alternative arrangement if the repair is likely to take more than five (5) working days.

5.5 The Contractor shall comply with all applicable safety regulations and Site-specific rules while performing the Services. The Contractor shall ensure that its personnel are adequately trained and equipped, and shall carry appropriate insurance cover for the duration of this Agreement.

6. PERFORMANCE METRICS AND REPORTING

6.1 The Contractor shall meet the following performance metrics:

(a) Monthly energy consumption reports shall be submitted within ten (10) working days of the end of each calendar month;

(b) Quarterly energy performance reviews shall be conducted within fifteen (15) working days of the end of each quarter;
